  "applicability_scope": [
    "Level 1 review by Shuangping Li on 13 November 2026 of the eight P23 arXiv v2 Results/Overview.lean claim aliases, with AI-assisted statement translations. The P23 module and its shared Support/KleinbergWei topology are unchanged between the reviewed checkpoint 6062058 and the baseline 43a61da.",
    "Definitions 3.1-3.2 and Claim 3.3: for window bounds g <= f (nondecreasing, values in Nat with top, all at least 1), the lower f-window density of any set is at most its lower g-window density; densities are valued in ENNReal and window starts satisfy m >= 1.",
    "Claim 3.5: lower Banach density equals the infimum of lower window densities over all window bounds.",
    "Perfect-tower definition and Claim 3.6: a member of the collection is a limit point of the containment topology exactly when it is the terminal language of an infinite perfect tower; the supplied enumeration only excludes the empty terminal language.",
    "Claims 4.4 and 7.1: for nondecreasing f : Nat -> Nat, zero-based niceness is equivalent to unboundedness.",
    "Claim 4.11 in its repaired form: in a collection of finite Cantor-Bendixson rank, a convergent sequence of proper subsets of K eventually has rank strictly below the rank of K. The printed claim omits J_j != K and is false for the constant sequence.",
    "Claim 4.18: the prefix-LCA change-index cardinality bound in any meet-semilattice with a strictly monotone natural depth bounded at the first vertex.",
    "Claim 4.20: under Mathlib rooted-tree classes, some adjacent pair of any vertex sequence of length at least two realizes the overall LCA.",
    "Recursive project-local statement-relevant definitions, including window counts, ratios, minima and densities, window bounds, the containment topology, finite Cantor-Bendixson derivatives and ranks, perfect and convergent proper towers, niceness, and the prefix-LCA definitions."
  ],
  "not_automatically_tracked": [
